                <pb facs="0498" n="416" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg416"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/898.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-03-08T17:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1911—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s March 7, 10 p.m. Minister for foreign affairs much gratified to have
                    President’s assurance, but states no misgivings were entertained. The
                    mobilization is to-day the preponderating topic in all circles, the general
                    opinion being that it has some ulterior purpose.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dearing.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
